Package: localvspp
Type: Package
Title: Multi-Resolution Local Variable Selection for Spatial Point Processes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Debjoy", "Thakur", email = "debjoythakur@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Localized variable selection for the intensity of inhomogeneous
    Poisson point processes. Covariates are smoothed to a Berman-Turner
    quadrature scheme, interacted with two-dimensional Haar wavelet atoms,
    and fitted by penalized Poisson regression (LASSO, adaptive LASSO and
    SCAD via local linear approximation) with the tuning parameter chosen
    by a composite BIC. The result shows which predictors matter, where,
    and at what spatial scale. Global (non-localized) counterparts are
    provided for comparison, together with post-selection evaluation and
    plotting tools. Ships St. Louis crime events with high-dimensional
    built-environment features as example data.
